MathJax-Newcm font for MathJax (@mathjax/mathjax-newcm-font 4.1.3)
====================================================================

Files: svg/dynamic/*.js, the 40 dynamic font files of the npm package
@mathjax/mathjax-newcm-font 4.1.3, copied unmodified from
https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@mathjax/mathjax-newcm-font@4.1.3/svg/dynamic/
(each one checked against the sha256 that jsDelivr publishes). The base
glyphs of the same font are built into ../mathjax/tex-svg.js.

Two licenses apply:

- The JavaScript packaging (the code that registers the data with MathJax)
  is by MathJax, Inc. and the package declares the Apache License 2.0
  (LICENSE in this directory; the package ships no license file of its own).

- The glyph outline data is derived from the New Computer Modern fonts,
  (C) 2019-2021 Antonis Tsolomitis, released under the GUST Font License
  (GUST-FONT-LICENSE.txt), which is the LaTeX Project Public License,
  version 1.3c or later (LPPL-1.3c.txt), plus a non-binding request to
  rename derived fonts. The package's own .woff2 files state this in their
  name table: "Copyright (c) 2024 MathJax, Inc. ... Original copyright:
  (C) 2019-2021 Antonis Tsolomitis. This work is released under the GUST
  Font License".

  This is a modified version of New Computer Modern: MathJax converted the
  glyphs to SVG path data and renamed the font (MathJaxNewcm). These files
  are redistributed here as MathJax published them, without further
  changes. The unmodified original fonts are available on CTAN as the
  package `newcomputermodern` (https://ctan.org/pkg/newcomputermodern).
  Redistributing it here implies no support from the original author;
  questions about this copy go to the ZiraDocs toolchain repository.
